  "notes": "Def Jam / Spoiled Rotten male soloist in the Tim & Bob and Hitmen-adjacent ballad school, 1996–2002. The research gives \"60–103; ballads 60–86 with the backbeat on 3\", so the ballad band is the base with `halfTime` true and a `halftime_3` snare. Three drum deltas quote the Tim & Bob grammar: \"kick on 1 and the 8th before 3\" at one or two hits a bar, \"layered clap/snare on 3\", and \"16th hats only under the chorus\" — a non-continuous lane at 0.15 fill density. The distinguishing fourth is \"tambourine on the backbeat\", encoded as a downbeat-placed tambourine lane with `tambourineMirrorsClap` true, which nothing else in this batch carries. Harmony is \"4-chord loops with maj7/m9 extensions\", so the triad share falls to 0.14 and the families run four deep; the entry marks its bridge-modulation claim `[LOW-CONF]` and there is no schema field for a modulation, so it is recorded here only. \"Light rasped tenor lead, harmony stacked in thirds, guitar lick countermelody\" is the mid-tenor register, the narrow interval spread and a counter at +12 with `answer_lick` leading. ⚠ Confidence is **low** — the research rates the entry medium-low and marks its key claim `[LOW-CONF]`, so the keys here are lane-level rather than named. ⚠ Every velocity, density and register number is INFERRED.",
